  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HealthAI: advancing responsible use of AI to improve health outcomes for all</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HealthAI is a non-for-profit Foundation under Swiss law, with a strategy that aims at advancing responsible use of AI to improve health outcomes for all, through governance and regulation. 
HealthAI intends to contribute to strengthening health systems and promoting responsible AI in health systems around the world. It will work to strengthen national and regional regulatory capacity for health-related AI solutions in LMICs, provide annual certification to regulatory bodies to ensure they effectively apply global standards, facilitate a global public repository of AI solutions in health, as well as steward a Global Regulatory Network and robust Community of Practice. HealthAI will thus contribute to increasing access to safe, high-quality, effective, and equitable AI solutions as well as trust, investment, and innovation in Responsible AI solutions for health.</narrative>
  </description>
